IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 400 of 2012
CITATION: (2014) 5 SCC 438
YEAR: 2014

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: K.S. Radhakrishnan, A.K. Sikri

PARTIES:
NALSA vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 14, Article 15, Article 16, Article 19, Article 21

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
third gender recognition, transgender rights, self-determined identity, affirmative action

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Recognized transgender persons as a third gender under the Constitution, upholding self-determination of gender identity as an integral part of personal liberty.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 14, Article 15, Article 16, Article 19, Article 21.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

